  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tanner leasing and factoring SMES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project aims to finance small and medium-sized enterprises (&#x201C;SMEs&#x201D;) through factoring and financial leasing operations in Chile. The proposed operation consists of a credit facility for up to US$60 million, an average duration between two and three years comprised of: (i) An A Loan of up to US$30 million to be financed by the IDB Group; and (ii) a B Loan of up to US$30 million to be financed by participating investors. The project will also enable Tanner to expand the financial services it offers to its clients, diversify its sources of financing, and, at the same time, improve the structure of its assets and liabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project aims to finance small and medium-sized enterprises (&#x201C;SMEs&#x201D;) through factoring and financial leasing operations in Chile. The proposed operation consists of a credit facility for up to US$60 million, an average duration between two and three years comprised of: (i) An A Loan of up to US$30 million to be financed by the IDB Group; and (ii) a B Loan of up to US$30 million to be financed by participating investors. The project will also enable Tanner to expand the financial services it offers to its clients, diversify its sources of financing, and, at the same time, improve the structure of its assets and liabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
